# Recipe for script/gather/lumberjack-enhanced.razor. Build it with: python3 util/build-scripts.py
# The blocks are module/<folder>/<name>.razor files, run in the order listed under #@ blocks.
# module/base.razor comes first in every loop without a #@ use line.
#@ output script/gather/lumberjack-enhanced.razor

#@ header
# Lumberjack gathering with self recovery, independent Tracking setup and one automatic Recall attempt.
# Needs: One Hatchet, bandages, reagents, recovery and harvest hotkeys. Automatic Recall needs a charged book with a Home rune.
# Tracking reuses a confirmed, active hunt color. Gathering waits for it, for a carried book and for a due Recall.
# Every 2 minutes Logs of all wood colors become Boards and go into the loadout looting pouch.
# For Tracking-triggered Recall, set Hunt Frequency to Always Get Closest in the Tracking window.
# Design and in-game checks: blueprint/lumberjack-pvp-handbook.html part 8.
# Optional cooldown bars: heal pot, walk, reflect. A missing walk or reflect bar cannot
# protect a cast from movement or reject an early Reflect retry. Check the active character.
# Warmode and an existing cursor belong to the player. Gathering and self buffs stand down.
# No attack, TK, summons, Meditation or automatic PvP-script switch belongs to this loop.
# A Recall decision stops gathering until this script is restarted. Sending Recall is not arrival.
# This script casts RecallCharge to Home. It does not walk to or enter a moongate.
# Server-event overheads and manual Tracking displays stay in the profile.
# The server blocks harvest for 60 seconds after Recall, Moongate, Hike, Teleport or Rope.
# The profile displays recent-travel refusals. The script does not read that message or restart the delay.
# The harvest retry only spaces attempts. It cannot shorten the server travel restriction.

#@ blocks
# Before the loop.
#@ use escape/tracking           sets the Tracking hunt filter once
# Every pass, in this order.
#@ use recovery/pouch            trapped pouch while held
#@ use recovery/cure             cure potion, else the Cure agent
#@ use recovery/heal             heal potion, else Greater Heal at the emergency line
#@ use recovery/bandage          self bandage
#@ use recovery/light-heal       light Heal, the bandage stand-in
#@ use recovery/refresh          Refresh at low stamina
#@ use escape/recall             one Recall on a Tracking report or low spare weight
#@ use recovery/reagents         reagent flags, read after the Tracking reports so it cannot consume one
#@ use gather/lumberjacking      Smart Harvest with the Hatchet
#@ use buff/spells               Reactive Armor, then Magic Reflection
#@ use buff/food                 eats from a tray
#@ use pack/lumber               Logs into Boards, Boards into the loot pouch

#@ config
#| Only the settings this loop changes. Every other setting keeps the default in its module.
#| Put the reason in "#" lines right above the value. util/build-scripts.py writes the "#|" lines.
#| Every setting of this loop: python3 util/build-scripts.py --settings recipe/lumberjack-enhanced-recipe.razor

#| ---- module/base.razor ----------------------------------------------------------------
#| 1 when warmode is the player's manual control window: our casts stand down while it is on.
#| Default 0. Read by recovery/cure, recovery/heal, recovery/light-heal, buff/spells.
# Warmode is the player's: recovery casts and buffs stand down, potions still go out.
@setvar! config__warmode_is_manual 1

#| ---- module/recovery/heal.razor -------------------------------------------------------
#| Missing hit points that cast Greater Heal when no heal potion went out on this pass.
#| Not below heal_hits.
#| Default 35. Read by recovery/heal.
# Bandages handle ordinary damage, so Greater Heal waits for 45.
@setvar! config__emergency_hits 45

#| ---- module/buff/spells.razor ---------------------------------------------------------
#| Minimum current mana to start Reactive Armor.
#| Default 4. Read by buff/spells.
# Buffs keep the handbook's 20 mana for Greater Heal and Teleport against a PK.
@setvar! config__mana_reactive_armor 24

#| Minimum current mana to start Magic Reflection.
#| Default 14. Read by buff/spells.
# Same reserve: the base 14 plus the handbook's 20.
@setvar! config__mana_magic_reflect 34

#| Missing hit points at which buffs are not started, and cut mid cast.
#| Default 35. Read by buff/spells.
# Buffs only while nearly full, so gathering never trades a heal for one.
@setvar! config__buff_max_loss 15

#| 1 buffs while poisoned. 0 holds them back and cuts one that is casting, so the cure goes first.
#| Default 1. Read by buff/spells.
# The cure goes first: no buffs while poisoned.
@setvar! config__buff_when_poisoned 0

#@ setup
# pack/lumber moves Boards into this pouch. restock/loadout picks it, this asks when it is missing.
if not varexist global__my_looting_pouch or not find global__my_looting_pouch backpack
    overhead "[ loot pouch, pick ]" 255
    setvar global__my_looting_pouch
endif

# loot/recycle runs the hotkey named in this list when it finishes or gives up. A list, because
# a variable cannot hold a word (blueprint/razor.html part 3). It lasts until the client closes.
if not listexists 'list__resume_script'
    createlist 'list__resume_script'
endif
clearlist 'list__resume_script'
pushlist 'list__resume_script' 'Play Script: gather\lumberjack-enhanced'

if config__sysmsg = 1
    sysmsg "Lumberjack enhanced v18 loaded: tracking color={{config__tracking_color}}." 88
endif
if config__chatty = 1
    overhead "[ lumberjack, on ]" 290
endif
